  "role": "Convoy guard",
  "summary": "A medium escort with a workhorse cannon, short-range racks and protected bins. Built to keep walking beside something slower.",
  "lore": "Sarn wrote the first Rivet conversion against a freight guarantee, not a military order. The surviving root could carry a better engine, but the carrier wanted a cannon it could feed and legs that could finish a shift damaged. The right gun cradle and left rack do not balance on the gantry; the counterweight is armour and the workshop keeps its measurements beside the root collar. Crews value the missile screen. The freight office values a machine that can stand between a stopped hauler and the reason it stopped.",
